92186049120 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1031 "Elementary Row Operations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1033 149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1034 0.3962220148324326 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049120 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "dc267e07-dc7a-5013-bcb3-616951f01683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428318 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1031 "Elementary 2x2 Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1033 1726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1034 0.639102274928378 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050576 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "54fffdff-21ee-5191-90e6-7d1d444eefd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186551768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113412 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f3cbf19e-29ab-5677-9980-cb6d9925144c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115075 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115075 #edb/ref 1071 "Let ![](images/a9/a9f425a48a3ed8fabfce0eb1785ebdddc62d7dd3208ac302fd66a89b03e58cdb.svg) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115075 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115075 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115076 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115076 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115076 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115076 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/11/11c345fde8fecb2e2a5459a0868ad8892e9067820de72f91601c1033858ca019.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115077 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4722" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115077 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115077 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ea/ead4157a19d725334c44a55903b52bd12d7627e73696c2100efee52340347468.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ba/ba70270430d6c5606e816c16c606c8f3940742a48c95b0ad8a33f6c935da8cf6.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186552422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186552450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186552453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115246 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861152