oduct That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115248 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115248 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1045 "Row Operations on 2x2 Matrices as Products of Elementary Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186116129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115473 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "16b40f91-5658-5189-b1b3-5c72e2c31649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186113412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32039" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a384818e-7ec3-5e40-9b82-69307830196b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115741 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42767" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd3b5a32-f5f9-54aa-b2af-a91ccc349130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115843 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186116129 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116129 #edb/ref 1061 17226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116129 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7bbedb9-6a2a-55a3-b430-2e2720918232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116129 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116130 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116130 #edb/ref 1061 17227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116130 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c86254d-65d6-53f5-80cb-058b8e3bc172" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116130 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116131 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116131 #edb/ref 1061 17228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116131 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3eb5a2ce-3bcb-5884-a872-6bd15f8824da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116131 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116132 #edb/ref 1061 17229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116132 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a0e9919-2a74-5681-a749-2ab1434ad705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116132 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116497 #edb/ref 1064 "To compute the product of an elementary matrix and another matrix, one option is to perform the matrix multiplication as usual. However, there's an easier, quicker way.\n\nRemember that every elementary matrix is the result of applying an elementary row operation to the identity matrix. If we multiply another matrix by an elementary matrix, we're effectively applying the elementary row operation to the other matrix.\n\nFor example, suppose we are asked to find the product $EA$ where\n![](images/25/25d4c31649834fe3ae42a701d49f6e4a31fa8626de1d9aeed0f98ccbbf4a57fb.svg)\n\nThe elementary matrix $E$ comes from swapping the two rows of the identity matrix ($R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$). So, to compute the product $EA,$ all we have to do is swap the two rows of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/49/497b76accb211bbe4253ee2094206f70e8856f9510db71f6367f255fcc565665.svg)\n\nThis may seem almost too easy. But it's true! And we can verify it by computing the product the long way, using matrix multiplication. Indeed, we get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we say that $E \\cdot A$ is equivalent to applying to $A$ the elementary row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$\n\n**Watch out!** It's important to multiply $A$ from the *left*. If we multiply $A$ by an elementary matrix from the *right*, we will perform a *column* operation on $A$ (not a row operation). In this case, multiplying $A$ by $E$ from the right will have the effect of switching the *columns* of $A,$ not the rows.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AE & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116497 #edb/ref 1065 3166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116497 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "527d3bb7-567f-5115-ad1c-31bd81fe1c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116497 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263022 #edb/ref 1080 "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186263022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "029edf87-92f0-5f4d-857c-fbcd96d1ad44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263044 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186263044 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263044 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04c58135-ba05-51f9-b009-72ffcc1bed2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263284 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ef7082b-a8cb-5f1a-919c-08c1470cb74b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263335 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263335 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263335 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26826c57-252e-56f3-928a-7ed1b119d8ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264117 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:=-5{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264117 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264117 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81bc10fa-ce64-5073-9d1d-50f07fae01cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264255 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186264255 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264255 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "92720e0d-2494-5493-a17f-d03095b968db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264401 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186264401 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264401 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a462712d-421d-50ca-982e-193a070b7aea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264461 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264461 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264461 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aac4da94-090c-5cac-8faf-9b696938bf0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264983 #edb/ref 1080 "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186264983 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264983 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e44c943e-a381-50e6-92bb-55c088607ad0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265138 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f36fc7b0-5e82-5868-91c8-65280ba1adb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186263044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265615 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d138b62f-6f1b-544f-a0dd-55662c209a48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263335